# The national unit for china. Items take n=4; the world items reviewed here change by level.
# Dates are in engine/notation/chronicle.ts with their sources.
lesson history-g5-china-our-country-in-its-time v=1 format=teach grade=5 unit=9 subject=history nation=china levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Great works of water and stone"
  goal "Put China's great ancient works in order, count the years between them, and say why they were built."

  look {
    scene 36x9 {
      timeline line from=-300 to=700 step=125 years=[-256, 600, 609] labels=["Dujiangyan built", "Anji bridge built", "Grand Canal completed"] at=canvas(0, 0)
    }
    say """
      Around 256 BC the state of Qin built Dujiangyan on the river Min, a system that still waters the fields of Sichuan and holds back floods. Between 595 and 605 the craftsman Li Chun built the Anji bridge, the oldest stone arch bridge of its kind still standing. In 609 the Grand Canal was completed, carrying grain from the south to the north.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked history.n5-what n=4
    }
    show history.n5-order n=4 k=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2
    show history.n5-between n=4 k=0 hard-k=1
    show history.n5-century n=4 k=0 hard-k=1
    show history.voyage-order k=2 easy-k=0 hard-k=4
    show history.continent-letter k=2 easy-k=0 hard-k=4
    show history.print-order k=2 easy-k=0 hard-k=4
    show history.n5-order n=4 k=2 easy-k=1 hard-k=0
    level medium hard {
      show history.n5-what n=4
    }
    level easy {
      show history.n5-century n=4 k=1
    }
    level hard {
      show history.voyage-order k=5
    }
  }
  story {
    show history.n5-between n=4 k=1 hard-k=0
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show history.n5-why n=4
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show history.n5-find-out n=4
  }
  remember {
    say "Every date in our country's story can be put on the line and counted from, and every one came from a source."
  }

  grown-ups """
    The idea is to use the grade's methods (timelines across year one, centuries, sources) on a
    chapter of the family's own country. The way in names what a thing was; the core orders three
    events, counts the years between two, names a century, and reviews voyages, continents and
    printing; the two-star question asks why something was done. If the child is stuck on
    counting, count to the next hundred first. The three-star task is for you to mark: a small
    piece of finding out with you. China's 道德与法治 for grade five has a lesson on 「古代科技 耀我中华」, with China's ancient works of science and engineering (the 统编版 textbook's lesson title; the 2022 standard itself was not read).
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level a worked example says what the thing was, the events come nearly in order, the years counted are the closest pair, and the review questions are the plainest."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the events are fully muddled, the years counted are the longer pair, the century asked has a trap, and the review questions cross year one."
  }
}
